Changes made for dvdnav.library (formerly amcedvd.library) to libdvdread 7.1.1 and
libdvdnav 7.0.0, as released by VideoLAN (Ubuntu's orig tarballs,
SHA-256 a0d47876548bec806774bbf8dbf20bb19ba139464383156b32eb8e59915b90a9
and a2a18f5ad36d133c74bf9106b6445806fa253b09141a46392550394b647b221e).
Only src/, AUTHORS, COPYING and README.md are kept; meson's build files
are replaced by the Makefile and src/port.

14 November 2026, Brian King:

libdvdread/src/dvd_input.c, file_seek():
    the stream's seek position is computed as (uint64_t)blocks * 2048,
    not (off_t)blocks * 2048: off_t is 32-bit on AmigaOS, and a DVD
    passes 2 GB.

libdvdnav/src/vm/decoder.c, eval_set_op() (the RND command), and
libdvdnav/src/vm/play.c, play_PGC() (random program playback):
    the random number is scaled with 64-bit integers, not float and
    double: no floating point is needed in the library.

Each changed line carries a "dvdnav.library:" comment.
